Experimental E2K (Elbrus) back end written by Claude
=====================================================

Everything under gcc/config/e2k/ and gcc/common/config/e2k/, and the e2k
hunks in gcc/config.gcc, gcc/configure.ac and gcc/configure on the
branch "claudes-e2k-compiler", was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI
model) as an experiment requested by the relcc2 project owner: build a
barebones GCC back end from the relcc2 specification (spec/isa,
spec/abi, doc/gcc-port-plan.md) to find out what the specification is
missing and what had to be guessed.

It is NOT intended for contribution to GCC: GCC does not accept
AI-generated code.  The owner writes the real port by hand.

Build (see relcc2 doc/gcc-port-plan.md section 4):

  configure --target=e2k-linux-gnu --with-sysroot=<lcc>/fs \
    --with-as=<lcc>/binutils/bin/e2k-linux-as \
    --with-ld=<lcc>/binutils/bin/e2k-linux-ld --enable-languages=c ...
  make all-gcc

Link with lcc (it supplies libgcc, crt files and the C library).
